From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: defconfig: Switch system suspend off

Any system sleep resets the Radxa Cubie A7S: after a suspend to idle the
SPL banner appears again, nothing resumes and no reboot message is
logged. The firmware has no SYSTEM_SUSPEND, so the platform has no deep
sleep, and suspend to idle saves no power on its own.

Without CONFIG_SUSPEND, /sys/power/state offers neither "freeze" nor
"mem", the suspend request of a desktop session is refused, and nothing
can trigger the reset.

CONFIG_HIBERNATION stays, so CONFIG_PM_SLEEP and the system-sleep
callbacks of the drivers are still built. Switch CONFIG_SUSPEND on again
when the platform gets deep sleep.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: /sys/power/state offers only "disk", there is
no mem_sleep, and writing "freeze" to /sys/power/state fails.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/configs/defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
index 9ae084ec02d8..db1990a64112 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
@@ -89,6 +89,7 @@ CONFIG_NUMA=y
 CONFIG_XEN=y
 CONFIG_COMPAT=y
 CONFIG_RANDOMIZE_BASE=y
+# CONFIG_SUSPEND is not set
 CONFIG_HIBERNATION=y
 CONFIG_WQ_POWER_EFFICIENT_DEFAULT=y
 CONFIG_ENERGY_MODEL=y
